1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,116
When an n8n workflow fails,

2
00:00:03,176 --> 00:00:06,162
the red node is only the beginning.

3
00:00:06,222 --> 00:00:10,078
The real test is whether the cause becomes
evidence,

4
00:00:10,138 --> 00:00:14,430
the fix is verified, and the same failure
stays out.

5
00:00:14,490 --> 00:00:19,217
We will follow one recorded data-contract
failure from its original run

6
00:00:19,277 --> 00:00:21,393
to a tested input guard.

7
00:00:21,453 --> 00:00:24,439
Malformed input will stop before the
consumer.

8
00:00:24,499 --> 00:00:26,615
Valid input will still pass.

9
00:00:27,925 --> 00:00:32,890
Pisama closes the loop in six stages:
design controls, run,

10
00:00:32,950 --> 00:00:37,916
retain evidence, diagnose, verify the next
build, then prevent recurrence.

11
00:00:39,925 --> 00:00:44,366
The release harness begins with nineteen
source-backed n8n executions:

12
00:00:44,426 --> 00:00:48,868
healthy runs and known failures labeled
from their records.

13
00:00:48,928 --> 00:00:51,368
Eighteen form the regression set;

14
00:00:51,428 --> 00:00:53,869
one holdout is sealed separately.

15
00:00:53,929 --> 00:00:55,870
I run the workflow.

16
00:00:55,930 --> 00:01:00,871
Pisama evaluates each trace and retains a
stable case identity.

17
00:01:00,931 --> 00:01:04,373
The retention branch prevents repeat runs
from

18
00:01:04,433 --> 00:01:06,373
creating duplicate Pisama executions.

19
00:01:08,925 --> 00:01:10,927
Now we have evidence.

20
00:01:10,987 --> 00:01:16,598
This execution reached the consumer
without body dot required dot value,

21
00:01:16,658 --> 00:01:19,691
and n8n recorded the failed expression.

22
00:01:19,751 --> 00:01:23,816
Pisama retains the workflow, node, trace,
expected label,

23
00:01:23,876 --> 00:01:27,425
and detected result in one auditable
record.

24
00:01:27,485 --> 00:01:31,549
Reviewed evidence can then become an
evaluation case.

25
00:01:33,425 --> 00:01:38,189
A second case shows sixty-four seconds
against a thirty-second limit.

26
00:01:38,249 --> 00:01:42,049
Pisama identifies the timeout and Slow
Code as

27
00:01:42,109 --> 00:01:43,979
the last executed node.

28
00:01:44,039 --> 00:01:47,839
The trace retains the measured duration
and limit.

29
00:01:47,899 --> 00:01:52,181
The operator reviews the evidence before
any control changes.

30
00:01:52,241 --> 00:01:54,111
Diagnosis informs the decision.

31
00:01:54,171 --> 00:01:57,488
It does not silently rewrite the workflow.

32
00:01:58,748 --> 00:02:02,977
The next build runs against the reviewed
corpus.

33
00:02:03,037 --> 00:02:05,658
Eighteen regression cases execute
asynchronously;

34
00:02:05,718 --> 00:02:07,802
the holdout remains excluded.

35
00:02:07,862 --> 00:02:10,483
Every expected failure set matched,

36
00:02:10,543 --> 00:02:15,308
with the build revision and each case
result stored.

37
00:02:15,368 --> 00:02:17,453
Label corrections append evidence.

38
00:02:17,513 --> 00:02:19,597
Earlier scores remain unchanged.

39
00:02:19,657 --> 00:02:22,814
Each scored row preserves its revision,

40
00:02:22,874 --> 00:02:25,494
expected modes, and exact-match result.

41
00:02:27,248 --> 00:02:31,592
For the contract failure, Pisama proposes
a deterministic input

42
00:02:31,652 --> 00:02:33,549
guard for operator review.

43
00:02:33,609 --> 00:02:38,932
The proposal names the failing consumer
and stays under human review.

44
00:02:38,992 --> 00:02:42,357
Two real requests test the installed
guard.

45
00:02:42,417 --> 00:02:45,293
Malformed input stops before the consumer.

46
00:02:45,353 --> 00:02:46,761
Valid input passes.

47
00:02:46,821 --> 00:02:50,675
Both results remain attached to the repair
record.

48
00:02:50,735 --> 00:02:54,590
Rollback restores the workflow and
preserves verification history.

49
00:02:56,748 --> 00:03:02,034
The chain now connects failure evidence to
a reviewed diagnosis,

50
00:03:02,094 --> 00:03:05,777
an auditable release, and a preventive
control.

51
00:03:05,837 --> 00:03:08,985
For teams operating critical n8n
workflows,

52
00:03:09,045 --> 00:03:11,123
incidents become reusable safeguards.

53
00:03:11,183 --> 00:03:12,727
See what failed.

54
00:03:12,787 --> 00:03:14,331
Prove the fix.

55
00:03:14,391 --> 00:03:15,400
Prevent recurrence.

56
00:03:15,460 --> 00:03:17,004
Pisama dot ai.
